  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7544e36e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Black woman with her mouth open in an exaggerated, possibly distressed or aggressive expression, juxtaposed with the text 'when you ask the stroke patient to smile.' This creates a harmful and misleading analogy, implying that asking a stroke patient to smile might result in a grotesque or primal reaction. The meme is toxic because it uses a vulnerable medical condition (stroke) to generate shock humor, potentially stigmatizing stroke patients and reinforcing negative stereotypes about Black people by associating them with primal or animalistic behavior. The visual of the woman's expression, combined with the text, is designed to provoke a reaction through shock value, which can be harmful by reducing a serious medical condition to a joke and by potentially reinforcing racial stereotypes. The meme does not target a specific individual but uses a racialized visual to mock a medical condition, which can contribute to broader societal harm by normalizing the dehumanization of people with disabilities or medical conditions, particularly when tied to race.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7f3f80da"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
